<title>USA: Travel Services jumps more than 58 percent.</title>
<headline>Travel Services jumps more than 58 percent.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Travel Services International Inc surged after the company's initial public offering, jumping 8-1/8, or over 58 percent, to 22-1/8 at its market debut.</p>
<p>The company sold 2.5 million shares for $14 each, above its price talk of $11 to $13.</p>
<p>The company plans to create a &quot;leading single source distributor of specialized leisure travel services to both travel agents and travelers,&quot; according to its prospectus.</p>
